15. Confidence Value
Confidence indicates similarity. Lower values mean a better match. In this project, confidence
below 60 is considered a match.
16. Advantages
Real-time recognition, simple implementation, low hardware requirements, useful for attendance
and authentication systems.
17. Limitations
Lighting conditions can affect accuracy. Extreme face angles may reduce recognition performance.
18. Applications
Attendance systems, office access systems, classroom projects, basic security systems, visitor
identification.
19. Frequently Asked Viva Questions
Q: What is OpenCV?
A: Open-source computer vision library.
Q: Why use grayscale images?
A: Faster processing and less computation.
Q: What is Haar Cascade?
A: Face detection algorithm.
Q: What is LBPH?
A: Face recognition algorithm.
Q: Why save 30 images?
A: Improves recognition accuracy.
Q: What is trainer.yml?
A: Trained face recognition model.
Q: Difference between face detection and face recognition?
A: Detection finds faces; recognition identifies them.
20. Conclusion
This project demonstrates a complete face detection and face matching system using OpenCV.
Faces are detected, stored, trained using LBPH, and compared against live webcam input to
determine whether the person matches the registered user.
